'''Coal''' is a fuel necessary to power [[Smelter|Smelters]] and [[Blast Furnace]]s while also being used by various crafting recipes.

==Availability==
* Dropped by:
** [[Surtling]]s
** Random [[Chest]]s
* Can be crafted:
** In [[Charcoal Kiln]]s using [[Wood]], [[Corewood]] or [[Finewood]]
** In [[Cooking Station]]s by overcooking any type of meat
** In [[Obliterator]], by converting items

==Usage==
{{Cols|2|
===Building===
* {{item link|Black banner}}
* {{item link|Coal Pile}}
* {{item link|Forge}}
* {{item link|Hanging Brazier}}
* {{item link|Mysterious Rock}}
* {{item link|Sign}}
* {{item link|Standing Brazier}}
* {{item link|White banner}}
* {{item link|Yellow banner}}

{{List|Crafting|
* {{item link|Cape of Oden}}
* {{item link|Hood of Oden}}
* {{Item link|Pointy Hat}}
* {{item link|Mead Base: Poison Resistance}}
}}

===Refueling===
* {{item link|Smelter}}
* {{item link|Blast Furnace}}
* {{item link|Hanging Brazier}}
* {{item link|Standing Brazier}}

===Smelting===
* {{item link|Copper}}
* {{item link|Tin}}
* {{item link|Iron}}
* {{item link|Silver}}
* {{item link|Black Metal}}
* {{item link|Flametal}}
}}
==Notes==
* The ratio for smelting any metals using Coal as a fuel is 2 Coal for 1 Metal.
* It is possible to create "passive" Coal farms by venturing into the [[Swamp]] and digging [[Fire geysers]] down into the aquifer layer, making the [[Surtling]]s they spawn repeatedly take damage before dying and dropping their loot.
* The [[Ashlands]] are a great place to farm Coal, which can be easily transported to other locations using a [[Portal]]. Simply place a [[Wood Stack]] and ignite it with a [[Campfire]] or [[Staff of Embers]] to quickly receive 50 pieces of Coal per pile.
* By buying some [[Fishing_bait|bait]] and converting them in the [[Obliterator]], the player can turn 5 [[Coins]] into 1 Coal.

